# INERT. Every rule is commented out, so this file assigns no owners and GitHub
# requests review from nobody. Re-enable with:
#
#     sed -i 's/^#= //' .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Re-enable together with rulesets A and B, which carry
# "require_code_owner_review": true -- see .github/rulesets/README.md's staged
# path. Why it is off: perspectives/2026-08-09-explanation-in-the-wrong-place.md.
#
# Two mechanics this file depends on:
#
#   Last match wins, and ownership does not accumulate. A later, narrower rule
#   REPLACES the owners of an earlier one rather than adding to them. The
#   catch-all therefore names the default owners, and every rule below it names
#   the only owners for that path.
#
#   GitHub requests code-owner review when a non-draft PR opens against a base
#   branch carrying this file. No ruleset is involved and enforcement mode is
#   irrelevant. It reads the file from the BASE branch, so a project/* branch
#   has no code-owner review until main is propagated into it.
#
# Ratification is a human action (docs/ref/ratification.md). This file names
# which humans, per path. Tool involvement is never a byline.

# Default owners, applying only to paths that no rule below names.
#= *                                @subcontrabass @mrharpo @CameronRWest @MJWKagstrom

# The ratification surface: Status flips, number assignment, the index.
#= /records/                        @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /README.md                       @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /PRINCIPLES.md                   @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /TEMPLATE.md                     @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Governance discovery: what an agent reads before its first commit. The seed
# carries the same text under /project-seed/; these are the live copies.
#= /AGENTS.md                       @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /CLAUDE.md                       @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /.github/copilot-instructions.md @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# The seed is copied verbatim into every fork, so an error here replicates
# into repositories this corpus does not govern.
#= /project-seed/                   @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Enforcement: a PR must not weaken the checks that gate it.
#= /.github/workflows/              @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /.github/CODEOWNERS              @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /.github/rulesets/               @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Licensing: the outbound grant and the texts it refers to.
#= /LICENSE                         @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /LICENSES/                       @subcontrabass @mrharpo
#= /REUSE.toml                      @subcontrabass @mrharpo

# Explicitly unowned: non-binding by construction, and gated on merge to main
# by the ruleset rather than by per-path ownership.
#= /perspectives/
